{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 112, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e4 absent, removing e5 can leave node 3 fed only by e3 (or nothing), so the drop is far larger (exps 53, 54, 59)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 skip path, the e5 path carries more of the signal, so deleting it hurts more (exps 51 vs 52, 53 vs 54, 56 vs 57)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 3 lacks a direct input path, a conv on e5 restores a strong path to the output (exps 7, 9 vs 10)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With e1 removed, node 2 carries less information, so a conv on 2->3 adds little (exps 2, 4, 6 vs 1, 3, 5)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on e5 supplies the residual-like shortcut that is missing when e3 is none (exps 92, 94 vs 91, 93)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input->output skip where none existed gives a large gain, more than replacing an existing op (exps 21 vs 22-24, 28 vs 29)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the beneficial 0->3 skip with a conv removes the residual path, unlike filling an empty edge (exp 71 vs 72)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If e0 is none, node 1 outputs zeros, so a conv on 1->3 contributes nothing (exps 32, 37, 39 vs others)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If no